Yesterday morning I woke up very early.
It was very hot in the room.
Mumbai's heat was stifling and intense.
The fan was running fast, but it was of no use.
I looked out the window.
The sunlight was already intense.
I had to escape this heat.
So, I decided to go to the hills for a day trip.
I took out my own backpack.
I kept my water bottle in the bag.
I saw Asha's umbrella on the table.
But I did not take her umbrella.
I kept my own umbrella in the bag.
Then I put on my comfortable shoes.
I finished my tea quickly.
I checked my phone and wallet.
I locked my door.
I was completely ready to go out of the city.
